From 10f37548618564a5d82ea9bc2f85fb1f707e4f4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:40:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] SCUMM: Clear the hi-res text surface on single buffered
 games too

restoreCharsetBg() wipes the video buffer and then clears the charset
mask only when the screen is double buffered. That is enough for the
built in bitmap fonts, which draw into the buffer that was just wiped,
but the hi-res text lives in a surface of its own. On v0-v2, where
hasTwoBuffers is false, nothing ever cleared it and every line stayed
behind: in Zak two speakers with different colours piled up on the same
row and the glyphs turned into an unreadable grey and green mess.

Clear the text surface whenever the hi-res path is active.
---
 engines/scumm/gfx.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/scumm/gfx.cpp b/engines/scumm/gfx.cpp
index c54d709a..8353b9c5 100644
--- a/engines/scumm/gfx.cpp
+++ b/engines/scumm/gfx.cpp
@@ -1478,7 +1478,11 @@ void ScummEngine::restoreCharsetBg() {
 			}
 		}
 
-		if (vs->hasTwoBuffers || _macScreen) {
+		// The hi-res text lives in its own surface, so wiping the video
+		// buffer above does not touch it. Single buffered games (v0-v2)
+		// never reach the branch below and would keep every line ever
+		// drawn, one on top of the next.
+		if (vs->hasTwoBuffers || _macScreen || isKoreanHiRes()) {
 			// Clean out the charset mask
 			clearTextSurface();
 		}
